                                    <h2><span class="shaft"></span>Microphone Parts S-25</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                     Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The S-25 is a medium-diaphragm cardioid electret condenser microphone, sold by Microphone-Parts.com both as a finished microphone and as a DIY kit. Billed as a workhorse microphone, it is suitable for most any studio duty from vocals to drum overheads.</p><p>Internally, the S-25 has a Transound TSB-2555 electret capsule that is coupled to MicParts&#8217; &#8220;ETL1&#8221; circuit. The ETL1 is based on the Schoeps CMC5 circuit, but contains MicParts&#8217; proprietary circuit enhancements. High-quality parts are used throughout:</p><blockquote><p><cite>Microphone Parts</cite></p><p>It uses 1% tolerance resistors, low-noise electrolytic capacitors, imported polypropylene signal caps, and NOS transistors &#8212; including an out-of-production JFET that is ideal for this circuit (due to its low capacitance). We manually &#8220;bias&#8221; every JFET in our shop to ensure that your mic has the highest possible SPL with minimal distortion.</p></blockquote><p>The S-25 kit has a heavy-duty &#8220;donor body&#8221; silkscreened with the Microphone Parts logo. The headbasket has a dual-layer mesh screen for a degree of pop filtering. Inside, the TSB-2555 sits on a custom U87-esque pedestal that is designed to keep the capsule as far above the mic body as possible, thereby reducing interior reflections.</p><p>There is one internal switch - accessible by removing the body sleeve - that can pad the the output down by 10db.</p><p>The kit is sold as an entry-level DIY kit for first-time mic builders, and can be assembled in about two hours. It comes with detailed instructions, a zippered mic bag, and swivel mount.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Microphone-Parts/S-25">Microphone Parts S-25</a></p>
